<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jos Plateau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jos Plateau is an upland region in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, rising to over 1,200 metres, with the city of Jos at its centre. It is home to many small ethnic groups who long resisted the 19th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> states around it. In the colonial period it became a major centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> mining.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jos-plateau.jpg" alt="Jos Plateau" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jiří Komárek · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hills_in_the_eastern_part_of_the_city,_Jos_(07).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
